Source: apt-downgrade
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: alanjmrt94 <alanjmartinez94@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 12), gcc, make
Standards-Version: 4.6.0
Homepage: https://launchpad.net/~alanjmrt94/+archive/ubuntu/ubuntu-tools

Package: apt-downgrade
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Downgrade installed packages on Ubuntu/Debian
 Command-line tool to find installed packages matching an exact
 version and downgrade them to a target version via apt.
 .
 Supports --dry-run and interactive confirmation before applying
 changes. Builds on Ubuntu 20.04 (focal) through 26.x (resolute).
